ECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 377163, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SC1PFbxknfqT5mGXxLeyev", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 381361, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` was rounding with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own comment says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `test_half_even` failed: it expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On the branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n- **PR:** #101 \u2014 https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory lookup, so the fix is based only on the test and the comment in the code. I haven't merged the PR; merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01R459zcDkttD67MDunPm4x4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018NcawvgkhBQ92pgiMbTvNH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P5AqKTsTESJgZBb6uaw724", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015zU9FqNHjSSAP4mE1uA6wV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", 